## Commands
Run from the repo root as `make -C services/__SERVICE__ <target>` (or `make <target>` here).
Same Makefile on Windows (recipes run in Git for Windows' sh). `make help` lists all.
- Setup: `make install` (uv sync → `.venv`). Add deps with `uv add` / `uv add --dev`, after
  asking the user.
- `make lint` (ruff, blocking) · `make format` · `make test` (pytest, no Docker).
- `make run`: API on the host at http://127.0.0.1:__PORT__/api/healthz.
- `make up` / `down` / `logs`: standalone container on host port `__ENV_PREFIX___HTTP_PORT`
  (default __PORT__). The whole platform: `make up` at the repo root (`run-platform` skill).

## Contracts
- Provides: `contracts/openapi/__SERVICE__.openapi.json`, generated by `make contract`;
  `make test` fails while it is stale (`tests/test_contract.py`). API changes follow the
  root `contracts` skill; the contract version is `API_VERSION` in `src/__PACKAGE__/app.py`.
- Consumes: _(none yet)_. Consume other services only through `contracts/` and the network,
  never their code or files.

## Conventions
- Code lives in the `__PACKAGE__` package under `src/`; imports are absolute
  (`from __PACKAGE__.config import settings`).
- Config only through `src/__PACKAGE__/config.py` (pydantic-settings, `.env` anchored to the
  service root). Container-network values go in compose `environment:`.
- Pydantic models for every request/response; every route declares `response_model`.
- Every feature or fix ships with tests in `tests/`, and `make lint` stays clean.

